OL,3,GNEWSATributes paid to dementia charity
OL,4,Aco-founder
OL,5,
OL,6,FTributes have been paid to an
OL,7,F89-year-old woman who helped start a
OL,8,Fdementia charity 13 years ago.
OL,10,FMargaret-Anne Tibbs was one of the
OL,11,Ffounding members of Bedford-based Tibbs
OL,12,FDementia Foundation, which now runs 53
OL,13,Fgroups with over 100 volunteers to
OL,14,Fsupport families across Bedfordshire.
OL,16,FShe started her career as a social
OL,17,Fworker in South Africa and in 1987
OL,18,Fbegan to work in care home, which led
OL,19,Fher to become a specialist dementia
OL,20,Fsocial worker from 1989 to 1997.
OL,23,APub: 08-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
